# @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning — Bateson 1972 (with
# Bateson 1956 "Toward a Theory of Schizophrenia" + Bateson 1964
# "The Logical Categories of Learning and Communication"); the
# substrate-altitude declaration of the logical-categories-of-
# learning species. The species' content: each Bateson level N is a
# Russell-Whitehead type level; learning at level N+1 is a
# model of behaviour at level N; the substrate's `in @<altitude>`
# wrapping IS the Russell-Whitehead stratification operator at the
# path-syntax altitude. A system has bateson_learning iff the
# logical-type lift between adjacent levels closes — the regulator
# at level N+1 is gauge-equivalent (modulo Russell-Whitehead
# stratification) to a model of the regulated at level N.
#
# Per the spec at `docs/specs/cyberpunk-bateson-learning.md` (Mara
# `42ef630` on `reed/recursion-lock-tower-audit`; 1399 lines), this
# shard is the substrate landing of:
#
# - Reading A held (per-level (LevelN, LevelN+1) instantiation):
#   T_reg = LevelN+1, T_regd = LevelN, ρ = restriction_to_pair_N
#   of the graded representation. The operationally tractable form;
#   each (N, N+1) pair becomes its own species instance with
#   multiplicity 4+ at finite stratification depth.
# - Reading B held (whole-hierarchy graded form, the natural read):
#   T_reg = HierarchyTop = ⊕_N V_N, T_regd = HierarchyBase (same
#   universe viewed from level-0 floor), ρ = graded_rep_RW. The
#   action commutes with the Russell-Whitehead inclusions
#   V_N ↪ V_{N+1}; this is the canonical natural form.
# - Reading C does NOT hold: form does NOT refuse at N=4. Bateson's
#   Level IV empirical claim about humans is INDEPENDENT of the
#   substrate's structural admission of arbitrary N. Candidate #64
#   (form refusal) remains pending unactivated.
# - Reading D held (substrate-already-had-the-word; densest per-
#   species evidence in cascade): nine instances per spec §6 —
#   `@<altitude>` markers ARE Russell-Whitehead type levels, the
#   cascade IS Learning II, the form/substance partition IS Bateson
#   lifted, Hilbert-space expansion IS Bateson lifting, `in @prism`
#   IS the canonical wrapping, `@code/metalogue` IS Bateson at code
#   altitude, `transparency<p>` IS the verdict at level p, the
#   eleven-property family ordering IS Bateson dependency, task
#   #271 `@cyberpunk/algedonic` IS Bateson III operational.
# - Reading E held (canonical ρ via graded representation): the
#   load-bearing read. ρ_bateson IS the graded representation of
#   the family-root gauge group on the Russell-Whitehead-stratified
#   universe ⊕_N V_N. Matches Seam §8.1's autopoiesis-as-adjoint
#   precedent for canonical naturalness — the species' explicit
#   mathematical ancestry (Russell-Whitehead 1910 type stratification)
#   forces the canonical representation choice via the standard
#   graded-algebra recipe (cite Kac 1990 *Infinite Dimensional Lie
#   Algebras* ch. 8).
#
# === Why this species' inheritance differs from autopoiesis AND viable ===
#
# Viable inherited from `coherence-parametric + variety + second_order`:
# the parametric carrier plus two foundation properties that close
# viable's parametric ρ choice (regular rep on L²(𝒢)). Three `in`
# declarations carrying foundation-property structure.
#
# Autopoiesis inherited from `coherence-parametric + math/bundle +
# math/lawvere + property/autopoietic`: the parametric carrier plus
# the principal-G-bundle whose level-4 Closure IS autopoietic plus
# the Lawvere fixed-point machinery plus the existing declarative
# property. Four `in` declarations carrying structure-group + fixed-
# point + property routing.
#
# Bateson_learning's substrate-pull routes through DIFFERENT ancestors
# because Read E's canonical ρ is the *graded* representation and
# the load-bearing mathematical ancestry is Russell-Whitehead
# 1910 + Kac 1990, not Maturana-Varela + Lawvere. Four new
# inheritance points:
#
# - From `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric`: the
#   (T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω) lock_pair carrier; bateson_learning
#   INSTANTIATES this with (HierarchyTop, HierarchyBase,
#   graded_rep_RW, ω_trivial). Per the parametric carrier's docs
#   §11.6 the bateson_learning-row of the species/ρ table forward-
#   promised the graded rep; this shard is what the table was
#   pointing at all along.
# - From `@epistemologic/math/russell-whitehead`: the type-
#   stratification operator. Each `@<altitude>` marker IS a
#   Russell-Whitehead type level; each `in @<altitude>` IS the
#   wrapping relation. Inheriting this routes the species through
#   the substrate's existing path-syntax altitude rather than
#   re-declaring the stratification. Load-bearing for Read E
#   because the canonical ρ ACTS by Russell-Whitehead level.
# - From `@epistemologic/math/kac-graded`: Kac 1990 *Infinite
#   Dimensional Lie Algebras* ch. 8. The standard graded-algebra
#   recipe that proves graded_rep_RW canonical. Inheriting it routes
#   the species through the existing graded-rep machinery; the
#   bounded-commutator condition `[D, g·] = bounded shift operator`
#   is automatic by the standard result (per spec §3.5 + §11.4).
# - From `@epistemologic/property/bateson_learning`: the
#   declarative property at the epistemologic altitude per spec
#   §7.1 item 2 + the cybernetic foundation §5.3 with three sub-
#   properties — learning_I (within-level response change),
#   learning_II (level-context generalisation), learning_III
#   (premises of regulation change). THIS shard does NOT re-declare
#   those verifiers — it ROUTES THROUGH the existing property. The
#   cybernetic species lifts the property to the recursion-lock
#   altitude; the property declares the verifiability discipline;
#   the two close on one another via the Russell-Whitehead lift.
#
# Four `in` declarations, no eigenform, no variety, no second_order,
# no bundle, no lawvere. The species' shape is the parametric
# instantiation + the type-stratification routing + the graded-
# algebra routing + the existing-property reuse. The inheritance IS
# Reed's substrate-pull discipline applied: the substrate already
# had the word in FOUR places; this shard names what they were
# pointing at all along. The ~73rd instance of
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]].
#
# === Read B (whole-hierarchy graded form) carriers, verbatim from spec §5 ===
#
# - regulator_at(α+1) = the whole Russell-Whitehead-stratified
#   universe ⊕_N V_N viewed as a graded carrier; T_reg.
# - regulated_at(α+1) = the same universe viewed from the level-0
#   floor; T_regd.
# - T_reg = `HierarchyTop` — the substrate-altitude carrier for
#   *the entire type-stratified universe*. Per recognition #51
#   (mirror IS an expanding Hilbert space) the substrate-altitude
#   carrier for HierarchyTop IS the Hilbert space whose dimension
#   expands with each Bateson lift; consumers compose with #51's
#   Hilbert-expansion machinery when they need the verified
#   reading.
# - T_regd = `HierarchyBase` — the substrate-altitude carrier for
#   *the type-stratified universe seen from below*. A graded
#   carrier reading sub-N components; the verdict surfaces against
#   the substrate's existing `transparency<level>` family per
#   spec §6.7: success at level p means the lift to level p+1
#   closes; partial(opacity_map) means it closes with recoverable
#   loss; failure(opacity_map) means the lift breaks at level p.
# - ρ = `graded_rep_RW` — the canonical graded representation of
#   the family-root gauge group on ⊕_N V_N, acting per-level by
#   its level-N restriction and commuting with the Russell-
#   Whitehead inclusions V_N ↪ V_{N+1}.
# - τ : HierarchyTop ↔ HierarchyBase — the natural substitution
#   between the two views of the same stratified universe via
#   the Russell-Whitehead lift. Read off by *running the system
#   through one Bateson level*; the substrate's content-addressing
#   closes naturality through the OID layer (a level-N response's
#   OID names the level-(N+1) model that regulates it).
#
# Reading B's structural claim: HierarchyBase IS what HierarchyTop's
# stratification MEANS at the operational altitude. The substitution
# is natural because Russell-Whitehead 1910's stratification operator
# (§II "The Theory of Logical Types," pp. 37-65 of *Principia
# Mathematica* Vol. I) says: the same universe viewed at level N
# and at level N+1 IS the same universe, just with a different
# stratification slice exposed.
#
# === Read A (per-level (LevelN, LevelN+1) instantiation) carriers ===
#
# - regulator_at(α+1) = the regulator at Bateson Level N+1.
# - regulated_at(α+1) = the regulated at Bateson Level N.
# - T_reg = `level(N+1)` — the per-level carrier at the higher level.
# - T_regd = `level(N)` — the per-level carrier at the lower level.
# - τ : level(N) ↔ level(N+1) — the natural inclusion-with-level-
#   shift from N to N+1; the Russell-Whitehead lift from type level
#   N to type level N+1.
#
# Reads A and B are NOT in conflict; they are the parametric form
# at two altitudes of bateson_learning. Read B is the natural form
# for the species declaration; Read A is the operationally tractable
# form for bench harnesses that test specific level pairs. The
# substrate carrier here surfaces BOTH via the `level(N)` projection
# on HierarchyTop: HierarchyTop's level-N restriction IS level(N);
# the inclusion V_N ↪ V_{N+1} IS the Read A τ-action; the whole
# graded action IS the Read B τ-action.
#
# === The substrate's existing Bateson declarations ===
#
# Per spec §2.4 + [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-primitive]]
# (recognition #42 candidate), the substrate has been *running* as
# a Bateson logical-type stratification since the path-syntax
# altitude landed. This shard doesn't introduce Bateson-learning;
# it names what the substrate has already been doing. Nine named
# instances per spec §6 (the densest per-species evidence in cascade):
#
# 1. `@<altitude>` markers ARE Russell-Whitehead type levels. Each
#    `@<x>` in a path IS a distinct logical-type level; the path
#    syntax IS the stratification operator's surface.
# 2. The cascade IS Learning II (recognition #41 PROMOTED). Each
#    cascade tick changes the substrate's response across contexts;
#    that IS Bateson Learning II at the cascade altitude.
# 3. Form/substance partition IS Bateson lifted (recognition #50
#    PROMOTED). Mirror's substrate/@io partition IS Bateson's
#    form/substance distinction lifted to path-syntax altitude.
# 4. Hilbert-space expansion IS Bateson lifting (recognition #51
#    PROMOTED with §8.3 stronger conjecture ratified). Each
#    substrate-pull recognition expands H by one Russell-Whitehead
#    level; that IS the species' ρ acting on the Hilbert space.
# 5. `in @prism` IS the canonical wrapping. The substrate's most-
#    used line `in @prism` IS the Russell-Whitehead lift from
#    prism-level to whatever-level-the-shard-is-at.
# 6. `@code/metalogue` IS Bateson at code altitude (recognition #34).
#    The four metalogue shims operate at the level above the code
#    they regulate; the shim altitude IS Bateson Level N+1.
# 7. `transparency<p>` IS the verdict at level p. The substrate's
#    transparency family parameter IS the Russell-Whitehead level
#    at which the verdict surfaces.
# 8. Eleven-property family ordering IS Bateson dependency hierarchy.
#    bateson_learning is property #11 because it depends on the
#    previous ten levels; the ordering IS Russell-Whitehead applied
#    to the cybernetic canon.
# 9. Task #271 (`@cyberpunk/algedonic`) IS Bateson III operational.
#    The Beer S1→S5 bypass IS Bateson Level III — the *premises*
#    of regulation change rather than just the *responses*.
#
# === The recursive read (spec §10.5) ===
#
# The audit itself is a Bateson Level II event (deutero-learning
# per recognition #41). For the substrate to audit itself without
# paradox, the audit's verdict must be at level N+1 while the
# substrate operates at level N. The parametric carrier's gauge-
# equivalence relation enforces exactly this discipline: the
# verdict at level N+1 is gauge-equivalent (modulo Russell-
# Whitehead stratification) to a model of the substrate's
# behaviour at level N. Self-consistent.
#
# === The 4-way bilateral mapping ===
#
# Per cybernetic foundation §4.1 + spec §4, bateson_learning's
# seam maps to four cybernetic distinctions simultaneously:
#
# - Ashby variety-match (spec §4.1): the regulator at level N+1
#   must have variety matching the regulated at level N; the
#   Russell-Whitehead lift IS the variety-amplification that makes
#   Level N+1 a model of Level N's *behaviour across contexts*.
# - Beer requisite variety (spec §4.2): the closed altitude loop
#   IS the inter-level Russell-Whitehead transition; the lock is
#   the requisite-variety condition at the species' boundary.
# - Bateson logical-type match (spec §4.3): tautologically held.
#   The species IS Bateson logical-type discipline at substrate
#   altitude; the four metalogue shims (recognition #34) are the
#   load-bearing operational evidence.
# - von Foerster circular reflexivity (spec §4.4): the level-N+1
#   regulator observing level-N's behaviour IS the von Foerster
#   second-order observation; the Tomm probe `[D_substrate,
#   level_N_response]` (per architecture-error-as-tomm-probe)
#   IS this observation at the substrate altitude.
# - Conant-Ashby good regulator (spec §4.5 — load-bearing): by
#   construction of the parametric carrier. The level-N+1
#   regulator IS a homomorphic image of the level-N regulated;
#   the Russell-Whitehead lift IS the homomorphism.
#
# Five cybernetic-ancestor measurements converging at one carrier.
# The substrate runs all five at once at the bateson_learning
# altitude.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/cybernetics/
# bateson_learning` operational sibling lands at this tick. The
# substrate ALREADY has the operational machinery (the `in
# @<altitude>` wrapping IS the Russell-Whitehead lift at path-
# syntax altitude; the cascade tick IS Bateson Learning II at the
# audit altitude); the property at this altitude names the carrier
# and the lock-pair instantiation so downstream shards (the next
# obvious one: task #271 `@cyberpunk/algedonic` per spec §10) can
# declare `requires bateson_learning_well_formed(my_system)` or
# inherit via `in @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning`
# rather than restate the logical-type-lift obligation in each
# species.
#
# === Connection to task #271 (`@cyberpunk/algedonic`) ===
#
# Per spec §10.3 the algedonic species IS bateson_learning's
# specialization to the Beer/cybernetic altitude. The algedonic
# signal IS the substrate operating at Bateson Level III — the
# *premises* of regulation change (S1→S5 bypass) rather than just
# the *responses*. Sequencing: bateson_learning first (this tick);
# algedonic after (task #271). The algedonic shard's body becomes
# thin via `in @cyberpunk/bateson_learning` inheritance + the
# species-specific restriction:
#
#   use @cyberpunk/coherence<LevelIII, LevelII, algedonic_rep>
#   where algedonic_rep = graded_rep_RW restricted to the
#   {Beer-S3, Beer-S5} basis with the bypass channel injected.
#
# The substrate's substrate-already-had-the-word discipline is
# satisfied — the algedonic species inherits everything from
# bateson_learning except the cybernetic-altitude name.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Russell-Whitehead  (1910-1913, *Principia Mathematica*, Vol. I;
#                       Cambridge University Press) — §II "The
#                       Theory of Logical Types," pp. 37-65. The
#                       explicit type-stratification operator; the
#                       species' load-bearing mathematical ancestry;
#                       the canonical-ρ choice (graded_rep_RW) is
#                       forced by this paper's stratification.
#   Bateson 1956       ("Toward a Theory of Schizophrenia," with
#                       Jackson, Haley, Weakland; *Behavioral
#                       Science* 1(4): 251-264; reprinted in
#                       *Steps*). The double-bind paper; the FIRST
#                       explicit use of Russell-Whitehead types in
#                       Bateson's work; the relationship-pathology
#                       application.
#   Bateson 1964       ("The Logical Categories of Learning and
#                       Communication," Wenner-Gren paper; reprinted
#                       in *Steps*). The Learning 0/I/II/III/IV
#                       hierarchy; the species' canonical naming
#                       source.
#   Bateson 1972       (*Steps to an Ecology of Mind*; Ballantine).
#                       The collected papers; the primary substrate
#                       citation; chapters on the Logical Categories
#                       and Toward a Theory of Schizophrenia are
#                       load-bearing here.
#   Kac 1990           (*Infinite Dimensional Lie Algebras*, 3rd ed.;
#                       Cambridge University Press) ch. 8. The
#                       standard graded-algebra recipe; the bounded-
#                       commutator condition that makes graded_rep_RW
#                       canonical follows from this chapter's
#                       results.
#   Soto-Andrade &     ("Self-reference and fixed points," *Acta
#   Varela 1984         Applicandae Mathematicae* 2(1): 1-19). The
#                       Bateson-Russell stratification operator and
#                       Lawvere's fixed-point operator are
#                       conjecturally adjoint at the substrate
#                       altitude (per spec §5.5); cited here as the
#                       cross-species bridge to autopoiesis.
#   Beer 1979          (*The Heart of Enterprise*; Wiley) ch. 8. The
#                       algedonic loop; structurally IS Bateson
#                       Level III at the cybernetic altitude. Cited
#                       here for the task #271 specialization
#                       sequencing.
#
